    "gold_solution": "```python\nimport math\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"VRPTW\")\n    m.setParam('TimeLimit', 300)\n\n    # --- Data ---\n    n_customers = 5\n    n_vehicles = 4\n    Q = 48  # vehicle capacity\n    vehicle_fixed_cost = 100.0\n    depot = [50, 50]\n    customers = [[24, 87], [66, 43], [78, 34], [54, 34], [35, 46]]\n    demands = [6, 17, 7, 24, 16]\n    time_windows = [[0, 308], [51, 149], [14, 87], [29, 87], [28, 114], [22, 97]]\n    service_times = [12, 10, 14, 5, 7]\n\n    # Node 0 = depot, nodes 1..N = customers\n    N = n_customers\n    nodes = list(range(N + 1))\n    cust_nodes = list(range(1, N + 1))\n\n    # Coordinates: index 0 = depot, 1..N = customers\n    coords = [depot] + customers\n\n    # COMPUTE distance matrix from coordinates\n    dist = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        for j in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                dist[(i,j)] = math.sqrt(\n                    (coords[i][0]-coords[j][0])**2 +\n                    (coords[i][1]-coords[j][1])**2)\n\n    # Service time by node (depot = 0)\n    svc = [0] + service_times\n\n    # Big-M for time linking\n    T_max = time_windows[0][1]\n    max_svc = max(service_times)\n    max_dist = max(dist.values())\n    M = T_max + max_svc + max_dist + 1\n\n    # --- Variables ---\n    # Arc variables (binary)\n    x = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        for j in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                x[(i,j)] = m.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f\"Arc_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    # Load variables (MTZ subtour elimination)\n    u = {}\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        u[i] = m.addVar(lb=demands[i-1], ub=Q, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Load_{i}\")\n\n    # Time variables\n    t = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        a, b = time_windows[i]\n        t[i] = m.addVar(lb=a, ub=b, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Time_{i}\")\n    # Fix depot departure to time 0\n    t[0].ub = 0.0\n\n    # --- Objective ---\n    # Minimize travel distance + vehicle fixed costs\n    obj = quicksum(dist[(i,j)] * x[(i,j)] for i in nodes for j in nodes if i != j)\n    obj += quicksum(vehicle_fixed_cost * x[(0,j)] for j in cust_nodes)\n    m.setObjective(obj, GRB.MINIMIZE)\n\n    # --- Constraints ---\n    # 1. Each customer has exactly one outgoing arc\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(x[(i,j)] for j in nodes if j != i) == 1,\n            name=f\"VisitOut_C{i}\")\n\n    # 2. Each customer has exactly one incoming arc\n    for j in cust_nodes:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(x[(i,j)] for i in nodes if i != j) == 1,\n            name=f\"VisitIn_C{j}\")\n\n    # 3. At most K vehicles leave the depot\n    m.addConstr(\n        quicksum(x[(0,j)] for j in cust_nodes) <= n_vehicles,\n        name=\"VehicleLimit\")\n\n    # 4. MTZ subtour elimination\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        for j in cust_nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    u[i] - u[j] + Q * x[(i,j)] <= Q - demands[j-1],\n                    name=f\"MTZ_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    # 5. Time linking: if arc (i,j) is used, arrival at j >= departure from i\n    for j in cust_nodes:\n        for i in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    t[i] - t[j] + M * x[(i,j)] <= M - svc[i] - dist[(i,j)],\n                    name=f\"TimeLink_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "Memo: Routing and Scheduling for Single-Trip Deliveries with Time Windows\n\nOverview\nWe operate a fleet of identical delivery vehicles from a single central depot to serve a fixed set of customers distributed across the service area. All vehicles depart the depot at time 0. Each vehicle performs a single out-and-back trip that starts at the depot, visits an assigned sequence of customers, and returns to the depot before the depot\u2019s latest allowable time. Travel time between any two locations is measured as the straight-line distance between their coordinates, with speed normalized so that one unit of distance equals one unit of time.\n\nRouting and Scheduling Challenge\nOur planning task is to assign every customer to exactly one vehicle and determine the order of visits so that:\n- Each customer\u2019s delivery begins within their specified time window.\n- If a vehicle arrives before a customer\u2019s window opens, it waits on site until the window opens.\n- Service/unloading time is performed at each stop; the vehicle departs after arrival plus service time (or window open plus service time if waiting was required).\n- Each route respects vehicle capacity limits at all times.\n- Each vehicle returns to the depot before the depot\u2019s closing time, which serves as the end of the planning horizon.\n\nOperating Requirements\n- Single trip per vehicle: Vehicles leave at time 0, complete their assigned sequence of customer stops, and return to the depot without intermediate reloading or multiple tours.\n- Time windows: Service must start no earlier than the customer\u2019s opening time and no later than the closing time. Early arrivals wait; late starts are not permitted.\n- Service times: Each customer requires on-site time to unload and confirm delivery before the vehicle can depart.\n- Capacity: The total demand loaded on any vehicle\u2019s route must never exceed that vehicle\u2019s carrying capacity. No split deliveries are allowed; each customer is served in full by a single vehicle.\n- Travel times and distances: Movement between any two coordinates uses straight-line distance; distance units equal time units for planning purposes.\n\nCost Structure and Goal\nUsing a vehicle incurs a fixed deployment cost in addition to the cost associated with the total distance traveled. Our goal is to design routes that visit all customers exactly once, meet all time windows and capacity constraints, ensure on-time return to the depot, and minimize the sum of travel distance and vehicle deployment costs.\n\nAnnex \u2013 Operations Data\n- Depot location: (50, 50)\n- Depot closing time: 308\n- Customer locations (with coordinates): Customer Locations (coordinates):\n  - C1: (24, 87)\n  - C2: (66, 43)\n  - C3: (78, 34)\n  - C4: (54, 34)\n  - C5: (35, 46)\n- Customer delivery demands: Customer Demands:\n  - C1: 6 units\n  - C2: 17 units\n  - C3: 7 units\n  - C4: 24 units\n  - C5: 16 units\n- Customer time windows (earliest, latest): Customer Time Windows [earliest, latest]:\n  - C1: [51, 149]\n  - C2: [14, 87]\n  - C3: [29, 87]\n  - C4: [28, 114]\n  - C5: [22, 97]\n- Customer service/unloading times: Service Times (minutes at customer):\n  - C1: 12\n  - C2: 10\n  - C3: 14\n  - C4: 5\n  - C5: 7\n- Vehicle capacity (identical vehicles): 48\n- Number of vehicles available: 4\n- Fixed cost per vehicle used: 100.0",
